Attribution for upstream data
-----------------------------

Data from Wikidata.

All structured data in the Wikidata main, Property, Lexeme and EntitySchema
namespaces is released under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public
Domain Dedication ("No rights reserved"). CC0 imposes no attribution
requirement; this notice is provided because the Wikidata community asks that
reusers credit the project, and because the ACL Rolling Review Responsible NLP
Research checklist (item B2) asks authors to name the license of every artifact
they build on.

  Source:    https://www.wikidata.org/
  License:   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
  Copyright: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Copyright

Snapshot identifiers, retrieval dates and file hashes for each benchmark
release are recorded in the release MANIFEST written by
scripts/extract_dump_delta.py. Note that Wikidata text outside the main
namespace, and Wikipedia article text, are CC BY-SA rather than CC0; no such
text is redistributed here.


Disclosure of machine generation
--------------------------------

The natural-language questions in this benchmark were SYNTHESISED BY LARGE
LANGUAGE MODELS from Wikidata triples, then validated automatically (SPARQL
uniqueness checking and contextual solvability verification) and reviewed by
human annotators. They are not human-written text.

This disclosure is made explicitly because OpenAI's terms of use permit the
redistribution of model output but forbid representing that output as
human-generated.

The model used for each released file is recorded in that file's metadata
block. Where a model identifier is absent from an older release file, treat
the generating model as unrecorded rather than assuming any particular one.


Intended use
------------

LiveSearchBench is an EVALUATION resource. It is intended for measuring
retrieval-augmented question answering over evolving knowledge, and is not
intended as training data. Training on these instances defeats the purpose of
a contamination-resistant benchmark.
